      "name": "bash",
      "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat > /workspace/src/component.py <<'PY'\\ndef calculate_black_area_doubled(A: int, B: int, C: int, D: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return twice the black area in the rectangle [A, C] x [B, D].\\n\\n    The wallpaper is divided by the lines x = n (integer n), y = n\\n    (even n), and x + y = n (even n), with the region containing\\n    (0.5, 0.5) painted black. Coordinates must be integers satisfying\\n    -10**9 <= A < C <= 10**9 and -10**9 <= B < D <= 10**9.\\n\\n    The doubled black areas of the unit cells repeat every four columns\\n    and two rows. From y = 0 upwards, the rows of one tile are::\\n\\n        2 1 0 1\\n        1 2 1 0\\n\\n    Signed prefix areas and inclusion-exclusion handle negative coordinates\\n    as well as positive ones, using only exact integer arithmetic. Time and\\n    auxiliary space are both O(1).\\n\\n    >>> calculate_black_area_doubled(0, 0, 3, 3)\\n    10\\n    >>> calculate_black_area_doubled(-1, -2, 1, 3)\\n    11\\n    >>> calculate_black_area_doubled(-1000000000, -1000000000, 1000000000, 1000000000)\\n    4000000000000000000\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    # prefix[row_count][column_count] within a single 4-by-2 tile.\\n    prefix = (\\n        (0, 0, 0, 0, 0),\\n        (0, 2, 3, 3, 4),\\n        (0, 3, 6, 7, 8),\\n    )\\n\\n    def area_to(x: int, y: int) -> int:\\n        # Floor division keeps remainders nonnegative even left/below zero,\\n        # so the same periodic prefix formula works in every quadrant.\\n        columns, rx = divmod(x, 4)\\n        rows, ry = divmod(y, 2)\\n        return (\\n            columns * rows * prefix[2][4]\\n            + columns * prefix[ry][4]\\n            + rows * prefix[2][rx]\\n            + prefix[ry][rx]\\n        )\\n\\n    return area_to(C, D) - area_to(A, D) - area_to(C, B) + area_to(A, B)\\nPY\\ncd /workspace && python tests.py; python -m doctest -v src/component.py\"}",
      "status": "completed"
    }
  ],
